    <instruction>Solve Rational Equations that Involve Functions</instruction>
    <exercise number="231" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <p>For rational function, $$f(x) = \frac{x - 2}{x^{2} + 6x + 8},$$ ⓐ find the domain of the function ⓑ solve $$f(x) = 5$$ ⓒ find the points on the graph at this function value.</p>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <p>ⓐ The domain is all real numbers except $$x \neq \text{−}2$$ and $$x \neq \text{−}4.$$ ⓑ $$x = -3,x = - \frac{14}{5}$$ ⓒ $$\left( {-3,5} \right),\left( {- \frac{14}{5},5} \right)$$</p>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
